# Build context exclusions for the API image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` into the builder stage, so anything not
# listed here is shipped into the build context and can land in a layer.

# Dependencies and build output — rebuilt inside the image.
# Critically, a host node_modules is arm64 on a Mac and would poison an
# amd64 build if it leaked in.
node_modules
dist
build

# Secrets. Never bake these into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# RUNTIME USER DATA — must not be baked into the image.
# public/images/ holds profiles/, proofs/ and celebrations/: real uploaded
# user content that lives in a named volume in production (~9.7MB today).
# Shipping local copies would bloat the image with stale user files.
public/images
uploads

# VCS
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Tests and coverage.
# NOTE: *.spec.ts files are deliberately NOT excluded. tsconfig.build.json
# defines no `exclude`, so they are part of what `nest build` compiles; the
# emitted .js is dead weight in dist/ but removing the sources from the
# context would change build behaviour for a trivial size win. The test/
# directory (e2e, separate jest config) is safe to drop.
test
coverage

# Local compose files. The production stack lives in deploy/docker-compose.yml.
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Tooling / editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.eslintcache

# Docs and scratch files
README.md
*.md
deploy-back.sh
test-websocket.js
